        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk94> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Evaluation criteria Offers will be evaluated against the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution; compliance with regulatory requirements; level of security; data sovereignty; quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI; total cost of the proposed solution; consideration of environmental issues; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk95> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The CHRB tender requires a pilot phase followed by progressive rollout to all services, with change-management support and staff training." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk96> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's PM methodologies and past public sector references, what is the best approach to ensure successful deployment and adoption of the AI assistance solution within the 5-year project timeframe? our company's hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure is well-suited for ensure. our company's can adapt our company's standard public-sector project framework to The CHRB tender, leveraging our company's past experience in similar deployments, such as the regional council and regional hospital group projects.  our company's will start with the Framing phase to define the project scope, followed by the Design phase to tailor our company's Atelier platform to CHRB specific needs. a pilot phase will allow our company's to test and refine the AI assistance solution with a limited set of users, before progressing to the Generalisation phase for wider rollout. our company's two-week sprints with demonstrable increments will enable agile adaptation to changing requirements and user feedback. our company's will also provide change-management support and staff training as part of our company's additional resources to ensure smooth adoption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk97> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Each phase will end with a formal review and a go/no-go decision, ensuring that our company's meet the project milestones and deliverables within the 5-year project timeframe. our company's joint steering committee and operational committee will oversee the project progress, and our company's single point of contact, the project director, will be responsible for coordinating the efforts and addressing any concerns or issues that may arise." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk98> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires response times < 2 seconds, 99.9% availability, API integration with SIH and DPI, support for health interoperability standards (HL7 / FHIR), and hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk99> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can our current technology stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do you propose to ensure seamless integration with the existing hospital information system? our current technology stack can meet the client's requirements for response times, availability, API integration, health interoperability standards, and hosting." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

